! <solver:p610_t3>
! Minimal 2-stage tunnel excavation (Mohr-Coulomb, T3 plane-strain).
!
!   Domain   : 4 m wide x 2 m tall, 15 nodes, 16 T3 elements.
!   Symmetry : roller BCs on x=0 (left) and y=0 (bottom); top and right free.
!   Tunnel   : 1 m x 2 m cavity hugging the left/bottom symmetry corner,
!              opened in two stages from the top down.
!
!   Stage 1 (top heading): elements 11, 12  -> upper unit square at (1<=x<=2, 1<=y<=2)
!   Stage 2 (bench):       elements  3,  4  -> lower unit square at (1<=x<=2, 0<=y<=1)
!
!   Mesh sketch (node numbering, y up, x right):
!
!     y=2:  11---12---13---14---15
!           | \ |  \ |  \ |  \ |
!     y=1:   6---7----8----9---10
!           | \ |  \ |  \ |  \ |
!     y=0:   1---2----3----4----5
!          x=0  x=1  x=2  x=3  x=4
!
!   Each unit square is split into two T3s: lower-right (i, i+1, i+W+1)
!   then upper-left (i, i+W+1, i+W), where W = 5 (nodes per row).
!
! <BEGIN:AnalysisOptions>
! failure_criterion MohrCoulomb
! material_type Isotropic
! mesh_type T3
! solver_executable p610_t3_mohr_coulomb
! <END:AnalysisOptions>
!
! <BEGIN:Header>
! nels  nn  np_types
16  15  1
! <END:Header>
!
! <BEGIN:Materials>
! phi  c  psi  gamma  E  nu  K0   (one value per line, per material type)
30
10
0
20
10000
0.2
0.5
! <END:Materials>
!
! <BEGIN:Mesh>
! x  y  (nodal coordinates, 1..nn)
0  0
1  0
2  0
3  0
4  0
0  1
1  1
2  1
3  1
4  1
0  2
1  2
2  2
3  2
4  2
! n1  n2  n3  (element connectivity, 1-based; 16 T3 elements)
1   2   7
1   7   6
2   3   8
2   8   7
3   4   9
3   9   8
4   5   10
4   10  9
6   7   12
6   12  11
7   8   13
7   13  12
8   9   14
8   14  13
9   10  15
9   15  14
! <END:Mesh>
!
! <BEGIN:Bcs>
! nr  (restrained node count; rows: node fix_x fix_y; 0 = restrained, 1 = free)
7
1   0  0
2   1  0
3   1  0
4   1  0
5   1  0
6   0  1
11  0  1
! <END:Bcs>
!
! <BEGIN:OutputNodes>
! nouts  (output node count, then node numbers)
6
2  3  7  8  12  13
! <END:OutputNodes>
!
! <BEGIN:SolverControl>
! tol  limit  incs  layers
1.0e-5  250  5  2
! <END:SolverControl>
!
! <BEGIN:Layers>
! Excavation layer 1 -- top heading (2 elements)
2
11  12
! Excavation layer 2 -- bench (2 elements)
2
3  4
! <END:Layers>
